    "body": "<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-requirements\">\n<p>You must be an Owner, Admin, or Manager to change the quiet hour settings for an account.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HP02CFHXBC9K2Q065XT8PB7X\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to change your quiet hour settings in Klaviyo, including: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Changing whether quiet hours are based on either the phone number's:\n<ul>\n<li>Area code (for the US and Canada)<br>Or</li>\n<li>Eastern Time zone </li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Updating when quiet hours are in effect for flow messages</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For more information about quiet hours, check out our <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/4408737146651\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">article on understanding quiet hours</a>. </p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HP02CFHXT93KCF21RQHEGSWK\">Before you begin</h2>\n<p>Please note the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Several countries have laws against sending during quiet hours.</li>\n<li>Quiet hours are only available for flows; however, you will get a warning if you attempt to send a campaign during quiet hours.</li>\n<li>Klaviyo does not set quiet hours on a daily basis. Your chosen quiet hours will apply to all days of the week.</li>\n<li>It’s recommended that you set up quiet hours so that flow messages are not sent between 9 p.m. and 8 a.m. in your recipient’s local time (certain states may have stricter quiet hour rules). \n<ul>\n<li>If you send to recipients in Alaska or Hawaii, either use quiet hours by area code or adjust the hours so that you aren’t sending between 8 p.m. and 2 p.m. ET.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HP02CFHXD3ABB8EPWB7GHRX4\">Change whether quiet hours is based on area code or eastern time zone</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Click your account name in the bottom left corner.</li>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Settings &gt; SMS &gt; Sender preferences</strong>. <br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/36748683955355\">\n</li>\n<li>Scroll to the <em>SMS quiet hours</em> section. </li>\n<li>Check the option you want to use for quiet hours:\n<ul>\n<li>Use phone number area code (recommended).</li>\n<li>Use eastern time zone. <br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/41370514460187\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-09-23 at 2.51.27 PM.png\">\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save </strong>to confirm your changes. </li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HP02CFHXZWH229EPSHZGPNBN\">Update quiet hours window</h2>\n<p>To adjust your account’s default Klaviyo SMS quiet hours:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to your account name in the lower left-hand corner.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Settings &gt; SMS &gt; Sender preferences</strong>.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/36748683960219\">\n</li>\n<li>Review the times listed for quiet hours.<br>The 2 times will represent the range that a message cannot be sent in the time zone being used. For example, you could adjust your quiet hours so that a message cannot be sent between 7:30 p.m. and 11:30 a.m. Eastern Time in the United States and Canada.</li>\n<li>Click the dropdown under <em>Stop sending</em> to change when quiet hours should start (i.e., what time the flow stops sending SMS).<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/41370503827099\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-09-23 at 2.53.07 PM.png\">\n</li>\n<li>Click the dropdown under <em>Resume sending</em> to change when quiet hours should end (i.e., what time the flow can begin to send out SMS).</li>\n<li>Once you update your quiet hours, click <strong>Save </strong>at the top of the page to save your setup.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HP02CFHXEGZBRRBAQVRHTZCA\">Additional resources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/4408737146651\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Understanding SMS and MMS quiet hours in flows</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005073907\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Understanding when and how Klaviyo sets a profile's location</a></li>\n</ul>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
